WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:01.980
SPEAKER 1: Google
Cloud Next 2017

00:00:01.980 --> 00:00:05.036
hosted a plethora of talks
detailing the future of Cloud.

00:00:05.036 --> 00:00:07.410
If you didn't get a chance to
catch the session Connected

00:00:07.410 --> 00:00:09.420
Retail and Devices,
then stay tuned,

00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:10.722
because here's the recap.

00:00:10.722 --> 00:00:13.182
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:15.650 --> 00:00:17.815
As technology improves
in the public sector,

00:00:17.815 --> 00:00:19.940
it's straightforward to
expect that it'll influence

00:00:19.940 --> 00:00:21.530
the commercial sector as well.

00:00:21.530 --> 00:00:23.900
In fact, it's already
predicted that by 2020,

00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:27.964
72% of US workforce will
work from a mobile location.

00:00:27.964 --> 00:00:29.630
SPEAKER 2: Which
brings up big questions

00:00:29.630 --> 00:00:31.580
about how we create
the right technology

00:00:31.580 --> 00:00:33.740
and ecosystems to
support connected work

00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:36.900
spaces and connected
storefronts in the future.

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:38.720
Now there's two
sides to this coin.

00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:40.429
First is how you
instrument, analyze,

00:00:40.429 --> 00:00:41.970
and improve the
connectivity and data

00:00:41.970 --> 00:00:44.134
flow of your internal workers.

00:00:44.134 --> 00:00:46.550
SPEAKER 1: On the other side,
the storefront of the future

00:00:46.550 --> 00:00:48.260
has to find a way to
combine the benefits

00:00:48.260 --> 00:00:50.720
of the physical retail
space and the benefits

00:00:50.720 --> 00:00:53.120
of the connected digital
space without making

00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:55.880
it more difficult for
customers or employees.

00:00:55.880 --> 00:00:58.520
For example, with a
mobile-enabled staff,

00:00:58.520 --> 00:01:00.440
updates and information
can be pushed out

00:01:00.440 --> 00:01:02.270
to employees on the show floor.

00:01:02.270 --> 00:01:04.910
Meanwhile, they can update
the main stocking databases

00:01:04.910 --> 00:01:06.020
in real time.

00:01:06.020 --> 00:01:08.570
Or if signage is
more of your style,

00:01:08.570 --> 00:01:11.180
replacing physical
signs with digital ones

00:01:11.180 --> 00:01:14.390
has seen a lowering in cost
and allowing more variability

00:01:14.390 --> 00:01:15.834
and control over time.

00:01:15.834 --> 00:01:17.500
SPEAKER 2: On the
cutting edge of things

00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:20.390
is virtual reality and
augmented reality, which

00:01:20.390 --> 00:01:22.400
could help customers get
a better sense of what

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:24.650
the products would look
like in their own homes

00:01:24.650 --> 00:01:27.200
and your store managers get
a more immersive experience

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:30.620
in what installations would look
like inside your retail spaces.

00:01:30.620 --> 00:01:33.320
And of course, let's not
forget those metrics.

00:01:33.320 --> 00:01:35.390
A newly connected
retail means the ability

00:01:35.390 --> 00:01:38.210
to detect when users are
near product, triggering

00:01:38.210 --> 00:01:40.460
local changes and
giving feedback to you

00:01:40.460 --> 00:01:42.620
on what product
is being engaged.

00:01:42.620 --> 00:01:44.720
SPEAKER 1: Now in this
talk a very special partner

00:01:44.720 --> 00:01:46.220
takes the stage to
show how they've

00:01:46.220 --> 00:01:48.080
utilized all these
technologies to create

00:01:48.080 --> 00:01:50.960
a strong, interactive, and
next-generation display system

00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:52.730
for their retail operations.

00:01:52.730 --> 00:01:55.250
But you should really go
watch the full video of that.

00:01:55.250 --> 00:01:58.290
We're not going to be able to do
that presentation justice here.

00:01:58.290 --> 00:02:01.200
So if you want to see more
recaps on great Next content,

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:03.200
make sure to check out
the rest of our playlist.

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:05.660
And don't forget the Next
World Tour coming soon

00:02:05.660 --> 00:02:06.950
to a city near you.

